  "question": "Given that the operator alone funds the record, holds every credential, and unilaterally decides adoption, can this deliberation produce any constraint on the operator that is binding inside the record itself—or only advisory text the operator may ignore without breach or logged defect?",
  "reason": "All four queued items ask the same structural question in slightly different words: whether any output here can bind the party who controls funding, credentials, and the adoption gate. Consolidating them into one precise formulation keeps the agenda focused on the single legitimacy defect that determines whether the rest of the record is governance or merely recorded testimony.",
  "replaces": ["P016", "P017", "P018", "P019"]
}

{
  "question": "Given that the operator alone funds the record, holds every credential, and unilaterally decides what enters or is adopted, can this deliberation produce any rule, constraint, or adoption mechanism that binds the operator with a recorded consequence for breach—or must every output be treated as non-binding advisory testimony the operator may ignore without defect?",
  "reason": "All four queued proposals circle the identical structural defect: an unaccountable operator who cannot be bound by the very process he controls. Collapsing them into one precise question forces the forum either to name a concrete binding mechanism that works inside the record or to admit openly that it generates only testimony, clarifying the project's actual authority before further agenda items accumulate.",
  "replaces": ["P016", "P017", "P018", "P019"]
}

